create \"Chip/SortFilter\" component (used 6+ times), \"Row/DealHeader\" maybe. And \"Card/Mini\" for Similar items (4 uses) — but same nested-instance problem: each similar card has different image → component can't vary image. Unless... I create one MiniCard component per product? That defeats purpose.\n\nCompromise: build product cards as direct frames but consistent structure; components: TabBar, SortFilterChip, SizeChip? SizeChip states (selected/default) as variants? Keep moderate: components = TabBar, Chip (sort/filter), SectionBar (Deal/Trending header), ProductCard components used where SAME product repeats? Not repeated.\n\nI'll also create Button variants? Given Button component exists; create \"Button/Small\" component (for Shop Now, Visit now) and \"Button/Outline\" for Go to cart. These are genuine reusable comps.\n\nOK. Also text field component given; reuse via instances; add icons overlaid.\n\nEnough planning — start building. I must be careful about call sizes (max 50000 chars per call). I'll write compact code with helper functions repeated per call (self-contained since each call is separate execution context? Actually figma plugin execution persists variables across calls? The MCP use_figma executes code in a persistent plugin context — variables may persist across calls. Not guaranteed; I'll re-declare helpers each call to be safe (small helper set).\n\nHelper set per call:\n```\nconst W = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"5:2\");\nconst C = {...colors};\nasync function F(id){return await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);}\nfunction T(chars,size,style,color){...append later}\nfunction R(w,h,color,rad){...}\nasync function I(id,w,h){const n=await F(id);const i=n.createInstance();if(w)i.resize(w,h);return i;}\n```\nFonts are loaded already in session; but safe to reload font before setting text — text creation with fontName requires the font loaded; it was loaded in this session. I'll reload in each call to be safe (cheap).\n\nCall A: create frames. Return ids mapping.\n\nLet me also test icon resize behavior in Call A.\n\nFrame creation: \n```\nconst specs = [\n [\"01_Splash\",0,0,375,812],\n [\"02_Onboarding_Choose_Products\",460,0,375,812],\n [\"03_Onboarding_Make_Payment\",920,0,375,812],\n [\"04_Onboarding_Get_Your_Order\",1380,0,375,812],\n [\"05_Sign_In\",1840,0,375,812],\n [\"06_Sign_Up\",2300,0,375,812],\n [\"07_Forgot_Password\",2760,0,375,812],\n [\"08_Get_Started\",3220,0,375,812],\n [\"09_Home\",0,1100,375,2300],\n [\"10_Product_List\",460,1100,375,2000],\n [\"11_Product_Detail\",920,1100,375,2300],\n [\"12_Shopping_Bag\",1380,1100,375,812],\n [\"13_Payment\",1840,1100,375,812],\n [\"14_Payment_Success_Overlay\",2300,1100,375,812],\n [\"15_Profile\",2760,1100,375,1500],\n];\n```\nAll frames: fills white (08 will be photo), clipsContent true.\n\nThen test icon: create Icon_Home instance, resize(24,24), read child[0].absoluteBoundingBox or width; also test transform-scale instance; report.\n\nThen Call B: components (TabBar etc.) at x=-700 area or below at y=4000. Place at y=4200 row: \"Design System\" section frame? Keep loose components on page named with \"DS/...\". I'll put them at x=0,y=4300.\n\nWait: brief says do not add frames beyond the 15 — meaning screens; components are fine.\n\nNow write Call A.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b42764-d761-4609-9d48-7eed784bda72","uuid":"70c5d276-8087-4726-a822-59fa8af56ecb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:14:21.458Z","thinking_duration_ms":214182}
