{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":67545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"04026ae534d40a7a14e54a196d190207","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: deal card images — I did weird resize juggling. Cards: deal card height 250 at y560 → ends 810... wait deal header at 486 h56 ends 542, cards y560 height 250 → ends 810, trending header 836 ok, trending cards y910 h220 → ends 1130. Then promotions below. Also within cards, overlapping: name at 688 (img ends 680). price at 738 or 712, stars 756. If desc exists: name 688 (h~15), desc 708 (26), price 738, stars 756 — card ends 810, ok.\n\nDeal images: `im.resize(170,120)` directly — distorts aspect (120x180 → 170x120). Distortion! Should crop properly. Portrait to landscape: acceptable to distort? It will look squished. Better: resize to width 170 keeping aspect (h≈255 for 120x180) then it overflows the card... With clipsContent, could put in a sub-frame. Simpler: accept distortion? Ugly. Alternative: make image area 170x170 square-ish? For 120x180 source at width 170 → h 255.\n\nOption: make image h=160 and resize to cover: scale to max(170/w,160/h) then center with clipping via frame. To keep it simpler, I could use frame container with clipsContent:\nconst holder = figma.createFrame(); holder.resize(170,120); holder.clipsContent=true; holder.cornerRadius=10; append im, im scaled to cover 170x120: k=max(170/w,120/h); im.resize(w*k,h*k); im.x=(170-w*k)/2, im.y=(120-h*k)/2 — crop center. That looks good.\n\nI'll fix the deal/trending images: find those instances and re-parent into holder frames with cover crop. Actually simpler to delete and re-add. The images are direct children of f with cornerRadius set. Let me restructure: for each card, replace image node with holder.\n\nHmm, but I can't easily identify which instances. They're at y=560 (deal) x=16+idx*178, and y=910 (trending) x=16+idx*158, width 170/150. I can find by position.\n\nFix in next call: iterate f.children where type INSTANCE && (y===560&&width===170) or (y===910&&width===150) → wrap.\n\nWrap: create holder frame at same pos/size, f.appendChild(holder), holder.appendChild(im), then scale im to cover: k=max(W/im.width... after resize(170,120) the aspect is broken already — but rescale ratio lost. Instance can be reset? The original component ratio known from media IDs: I stored IDs. Easier: delete those instances and recreate from component with cover math. Map by x position to media id:\ndeal xs: 16,194,372,550 (step 178) → ids 3:116,3:119,null,3:122\ntrend xs: 16,174,332,490,648 → ids 3:125,3:128,null,3:131,3:134\n\nDelete existing instances at those coords, add holders.\n\nThen continue with promotions section. Also fix category label x positions? Labels were centered at x+32 where x=16+82i — still valid.\n\nAlso banner: I resized Promo_Banner_Sale 300x120 → 343x137 (distort slightly, ratio 2.5 vs 2.5 — fine, 343/137=2.504 ok).\n\nPromotions plan (y 1150 onward):\n- y=1150: Special Offers row: circle image 60 + texts + emoji in title + chevron.\n- y=1230: Flat and Heels card: bg #F6F6F6 r10 w343 h84: image left 84x84 (Promo_Flat_And_Heels square → cover), texts right, Visit now button.\n- y=1330: Hot Summer Sale: image 343x150 (Promo_Hot_Summer_Sale 239x120 → cover).\n- y=1500: New Arrivals: title left 16 SemiBold + \"View all\" right; subtitle \"Summer' 25 Collections\" gray; then 2 image cards (use List_Black_Dress 3:146 & List_Pink_Embroidered_Dress 3:149) each 167x200 cover +? No names needed (not in DATA). Just images.\n- y=1760: Sponsored: title; card: image left 343? Promo_Sponsored_Shoes square → wide card 343x160 cover + text \"up to 50% Off\" overlay + name \"Sponsored\"? Sponsored card: white card 343x190: image 343x140 cover, row: \"up to 50% Off\" bold + arrow-right. Name it SponsoredCard.\n- ends ~1990; navbar at 2206; home indicator 2266. shell.\n\nFrame height 2300 — content ends ~1990, whitespace below before navbar. Fine, or trim frame to 2100. Let me trim after measuring. Home may scroll vertically — a bit of bottom space ok; I'll resize frame so content+~90 above navbar. Estimate: sponsored ends ~1990 → set frame height 1990+94(nav)+34(ind)+16 = 2134 → round 2140.\n\nThen 10_Product_List in next call.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b42764-d761-4609-9d48-7eed784bda72","uuid":"56add064-6060-41a8-9125-af12c624874f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:23:28.948Z","thinking_duration_ms":41317}
